# Files every slice only appends to merge by keeping both sides (docs/testing.md § "Landing a slice").
# A union merge keeps every line both branches added; the census lists end each entry with a comma so an append
# never rewrites the line above it, and `node bin/dev.js census --order-only` (run by `dev land`) restores the
# order a union may leave. The parity tests still compare the merged names with the generated registries.
docs/decisions.md merge=union
test/unit/census/RegisteredClasses.hx merge=union
test/unit/census/DeclaredArms*.hx merge=union
test/unit/census/DeferredArms.hx merge=union
test/unit/census/Pins*.hx merge=union

# JSON forbids the trailing comma a union would need, so the arm registry merges record by record, keyed by name:
# `dev land` passes the driver; elsewhere name it on the command line —
#   git -c merge.anyparse-arms.driver='node bin/dev.js merge-arms %O %A %B' merge <branch>
# Without the driver git falls back to its ordinary line merge.
test/testkit/mutation-arms.json merge=anyparse-arms
